From 06f3ede48c7bef6e092fd2f1277a3025667598a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 11:01:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/94] pmdomain: qcom: cpr3: look up the CPRh thread instead
 of attaching to it

Enabling both the CPRh controller and the OSM on MSM8998 hangs the SoC
before either driver has touched a register.  Seven flashes of DTB- and
cmdline-only bisect put the fault inside dev_pm_domain_attach_list(): a
boot that programs nothing at all comes up, and a boot whose only extra
work is that attach does not, with no fuse read, no CPR write and no OSM
write in between.

The attach buys nothing.  CPR-Hardened runs its loop in hardware: there
is no usable regulator (devm_regulator_get_optional() is deliberately
allowed to fail), the domain is GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON and its
set_performance_state is a stub.  Nothing calls a power_on, a power_off
or a performance state on it for the whole life of the system.  The
domain existed only to hand three things across: the CPU device, the
controller's own operating points, and the APM and MEM-ACC thresholds -
and none of the three need genpd.  The corner setup already reaches the
CPU's operating points by walking the device tree by hand, because the
required-opp linkage does not carry the frequency it needs.

So resolve the controller from the phandle the CPU node already carries
and call into it directly.  qcom_cpr3_cprh_init() now takes the CPU
device, finds its thread, installs and voltage-adjusts the operating
points, programs the corner table and returns the thresholds the caller
needs for the OSM.  The genpd is still registered, since it is what
carries the controller's operating points, but on CPR-Hardened it no
longer offers attach_dev or detach_dev: with no consumer attaching, the
callback would have dereferenced an acc_desc this SoC does not have.

The corner array allocation moves to a helper, shared with the CPR3 and
CPR4 attach path that still uses the domain the ordinary way.

While here, stop reporting success from qcom_cpufreq_gen_params() when
the operating point table came back empty: gpd_opp_cnt of zero fell
through the "greater than zero" test and was returned as a zero exit,
leaving the caller to fail later on an uninitialised entry count.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
